Why Is Demand Increasing?
Growing respiratory disease burden: Asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), and other respiratory conditions are increasing demand for effective inhaled therapies.
Advances in inhalation devices: Improvements in dry-powder inhalers, metered-dose inhalers, nebulizers, and soft-mist devices are supporting more consistent medication delivery.
Interest in targeted treatment: Delivering medication directly to the lungs can improve local drug exposure while limiting systemic exposure for appropriate therapies.

Pulmonary Drug Delivery Watch: Smart Inhalers and Inhaled Biologics
The market is moving toward connected inhalers that track usage and support adherence monitoring. Advances in particle engineering and formulation science are also creating opportunities for inhaled biologics, controlled-release formulations, and new drug-device combinations. Manufacturers must still address formulation stability, manufacturing scale-up, clinical performance, and regulatory requirements.

